  "overview": {
    "id": "overview",
    "x": 108,
    "y": 80,
    "width": 1330,
    "height": 150,
    "layer": -3,
    "movable": false,
    "movableInEdit": false,
    "css": "font-size: 25px",
    "html": "<b>layout</b> &quotrandom&quot scatters whatever is dropped into the holder. Every piece lands on a spot of its own with a small random tilt, measured against its size so nothing overlaps and nothing pokes past the border. A piece you drop keeps the spot you aimed for while it is free. On a crowded spot, it hops to a random free one instead. A widget taken back out straightens up again. <b>dropOffsetX</b>/<b>dropOffsetY</b> is the margin the pieces keep to the border."
  },
